changeFlags -- continue solutions of a Schubert problem to another instance
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        changeFlags(sols,CFG)
  * Inputs:
      * sols, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, solutions of a Schubert
        problem written as $n\times k$ matrices
      * CFG, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, a triple (C,F,G) where
        C is a list of m Schubert conditions, F is a list of m flags defining
        an instance with solution set sols, G is a list of m flags defining the
        instance whose solutions we want.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note OneHomotopy: changeFlags_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOneHomotopy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value true, strategy for moving solutions to a Schubert
        problem
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, solutions of the problem with
        respect to flags G.

Description
===========

If sols is a set of solutions to a Schubert problem $l_1,\ldots,l_m$ with
respect to a set of flags $F_1,\ldots, F_m$, uses parameter homotopies to move
$S$ to a solution set $S'$ for the same Schubert problem, but with respect to
another set of flags $G_1,\ldots, G_m$.

For instance, consider the Schubert problem $(2,1)^3$ in $Gr(3,6)$.

