Caveat
======

There are two strategies: when *note OneHomotopy: OneHomotopy, is set to *note
true: (Macaulay2Doc)true, (default) it uses straight line homotopies to change
flags, but assumes the initial flags are generic.

When *note OneHomotopy: OneHomotopy, is set to *note false:
(Macaulay2Doc)false,, it makes gradual changes in the flags by changing one
column at a time, and using only linear homotopies, but in this setting, it
generates polynomial equations using all minors of the incidence conditions
(thus is not very effective).

