changeFlags(...,OneHomotopy=>...) -- strategy for moving solutions to a Schubert problem
****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        changeFlags(...,OneHomotopy=>T)
  * Inputs:
      * T, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, when true [default]
        it uses a single straight line homotopy, otherwise it makes a gradual
        change in the flags, one column at a time.

Description
===========

There are two strategies: when OneHomotopy is set to true (default) it uses
straight line homotopies to change flags, but assumes the initial flags are
generic.

When OneHomotopy is set to false, it makes gradual changes in the flags by
changing one column at a time, and using only linear homotopies, but in this
setting, it generates polynomial equations using all minors of the incidence
conditions (thus is not very effective).

