checkIncidenceSolution -- check if a solution satisfies an instance of a Schubert problem
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        checkIncidenceSolution(s, P)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, An instance of a Schubert problem
        as a list {($l_1,F_1$),...,($l_m,F_m$)}
      * s, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, A matrix of size $n\times k$
        representing a solution to the Schubert problem P
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if s satisfies all
        the incidence conditions

Description
===========

For each pair $(l,F)$ in the Schubert problem $P$, where $l$ is a Schubert
condition given as a partition, and $F$ is a flag given as an $n \times n$
matrix, the function verifies if the matrix $s$ satisfies the incidence
conditions imposed by $l$ with respect to the flag $F$, for each of the pairs
in $P$, by computing the corresponding minor conditions.

Caveat
======

This function was created for testing purposes and will be deleted later as it
may not be numerically stable.

Ways to use checkIncidenceSolution:
===================================

  * "checkIncidenceSolution(Matrix,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note checkIncidenceSolution: checkIncidenceSolution, is a *note
method function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

