NSC2phc -- dictionary between different notations for Schubert problems.
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = NSC2phc(conds,k,n)
  * Inputs:
      * conds, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of Schubert conditions,
        either partitions or brackets, that constitutes a Schubert problem on
        the Grassmannian $Gr(k,n)$
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, $k$ and $n$ represent the
        Grassmannian $Gr(k,n)$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the corresponding Schubert
        problem in notation for PHCPack implementation of Littlewood-Richardson
        rule and homotopies. Its rows encode Schubert conditions with
        multiplicities. Each row is a $k+1$-tuple, {m,b}, where $m$ is a
        nonegative integer and $b$ a bracket (see  *note bracket2partition:
        bracket2partition, for details). The bracket $b$ represents a Schubert
        condition and $m$ is its multiplicity in this Schubert intersection
        problem.

Description
===========

A Schubert problem in the Grassmannian $Gr(k,n)$ is encoded by either a list of
partitions or brackets whose codimensions sum to $k(n-k)$. (see *note
bracket2partition: bracket2partition, for details on brackets and partitions)

The PHCPack implementations of the geometric Littlewood-Richardson rule encode
the brackets in a matrix, where each row has the form ${m, b}$ with $m$ the
multiplicity of the bracket $b$, which is a strictly increasing sequence of $k$
integers between $1$ and $n$.



