OneHomotopy -- strategy for changing flags.
*******************************************

Description
===========

There are two strategies to change flags: when OneHomotopy is set to true
(default) it uses straight line homotopies to change flags, but assumes the
initial flags are generic.

When OneHomotopy is set to false, it makes gradual changes in the flags by
changing one column at a time, and using only linear homotopies, but in this
setting, it generates polynomial equations using all minors of the incidence
conditions (thus is not very effective).

Functions with optional argument named OneHomotopy:
===================================================

  * *note changeFlags(...,OneHomotopy=>...):
    changeFlags_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOneHomotopy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- strategy for moving
    solutions to a Schubert problem

