solveSchubertProblem(...,LinearAlgebra=>...) -- switch between Linear Algebra and Parameter Homotopy
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        solveSchubertProblem(...,LinearAlgebra=>T)
  * Inputs:
      * T, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true for Linear
        Algebra, false for Parameter Homotopy

Description
===========

Chooses the method for glueing solutions from the top of one node (tournament
game) to the leaf of the previous node. When true (default), uses Linear
Algebra, otherwise uses Parameter Homotopies.

Caveat
======

Parameter Homotopies are not necessary and usually take longer than simple
Linear Algebra.

Functions with optional argument named LinearAlgebra:
=====================================================

  * *note solveSchubertProblem(...,LinearAlgebra=>...):
    solveSchubertProblem_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLinearAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- switch
    between Linear Algebra and Parameter Homotopy

